{
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "VO-01",
   "start": 0.06,
   "end": 3.04,
   "text": "He left a city a two-hundred-year bet. Guess how it ended."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-02",
   "start": 3.04,
   "end": 8.66,
   "text": "Seventeen ninety. A thousand pounds, about forty-five hundred dollars, goes into the chest."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-03",
   "start": 8.78,
   "end": 13.18,
   "text": "His rule: lend it to young tradesmen at five percent, and keep lending the interest."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-04",
   "start": 13.32,
   "end": 20.0,
   "text": "He did the math himself. One hundred years, a hundred thirty-one thousand pounds. Two hundred years, over four million."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-05",
   "start": 20.0,
   "end": 26.88,
   "text": "Eighteen ninety. The chest opens. Three hundred ninety-one thousand dollars. Only two thirds of his math."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-06",
   "start": 27.02,
   "end": 28.88,
   "text": "The man who made the bet? Ben Franklin."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-07",
   "start": 29.0,
   "end": 32.18,
   "text": "Part of it builds a trade school. The rest goes back in the chest."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-08",
   "start": 32.18,
   "end": 35.0,
   "text": "Nineteen ninety. The chest opens again."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-09",
   "start": 35.14,
   "end": 38.92,
   "text": "Almost five million dollars. Less than a third of what his math promised."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-10",
   "start": 39.1,
   "end": 44.12,
   "text": "Fewer tradesmen borrowed, many didn't pay back, and the money got parked in safe, slow accounts."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-11",
   "start": 44.3,
   "end": 46.66,
   "text": "The math never failed. People interrupted it."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-12",
   "start": 46.76,
   "end": 50.1,
   "text": "So could you leave your money alone for twenty years? Yes or no."
  }
 ],
